# Universal scan fixes (going live)

Aislix will soon be public. Customers will scan **any** shelf image, store, category, and planogram setup.

## Hard rule

When debugging a failing scan (or any production issue):

1. **Use that scan only as evidence** — inspect payload, metrics, logs, and mode to understand the failure class.
2. **Fix the underlying system behavior** so the same class of failure cannot recur for any future scan.
3. **Never** ship one-off patches for a specific `scan_id`, org, store, brand, sample image, or fixture path as the production fix.
4. **Never** tell the user that reprocessing one named scan is the solution unless they explicitly asked to repair that historical row; prefer a global pipeline/UI/API change and a fresh scan to validate.

## Examples of correct vs wrong

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|--------|
| Special-case `if scan_id == "ec140…"` | Fix parser / cache gate / prompt path for all AI Audit modes |
| Hardcode Lay's / one reference sample as the product path | Keep demo samples on landing only; product scans always use live CV |
| "Re-run this scan and it will work" as the only deliverable | Change backend + frontend so every new scan follows the correct path |

## When a specific scan appears in chat

- Diagnose root cause from that scan.
- Implement a **global** fix (all modes, all customers).
- Mention the example scan only to explain what was learned — not as the scope of the fix.
